# Do not invent

This brief describes what *should* be built. Verify the codebase before claiming anything exists.

Never assume or fabricate:

- embedding model, LLM, or reranker
- AWS service (EC2, Lambda, ECS, RDS, S3, Bedrock) unless actually used
- Redis, Celery, RQ, webhooks, private-repo OAuth
- dataset size, repo/document counts, users
- metric numbers (Recall@K, NDCG, p95 latency, cost)

Resume AWS wording is allowed only if it matches a real deployment.

Lexical search may be Postgres FTS or BM25 — check the code.

Workers, incremental sync, filters, feedback, eval dashboards, and private repos are optional/later unless the user asks to build them.

Do not add a queue/worker, AWS, or a new vendor just because the plan lists it as an option.
